{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`choosy-arthrodic-barbet` removed compaction from the close path because it held the ONE store\nwrite lock for up to 13m53s and starved every concurrent agent. That landed the P0 fix but\nleft the store with no standing compaction trigger: event logs now grow until someone runs\n`rebar compact <id>` by hand. This ticket restores an automatic trigger that never touches an\ninteractive session's store lock.\n\n## Approach\nTwo small pieces, both reusing what already exists.\n\n**1. Make `compact-all` recur.** The sweep is nearly built: `compact_all_cli`\n(`src/rebar/_commands/compact.py:213`) already enumerates ticket dirs, honours\n`--dry-run` / `--limit` / `--no-commit`, folds each ticket through the existing\n`compact_cli`, batches ONE commit + push, and reports compacted/error counts. Its only defect\nfor this purpose is SELECTION: `_scan_snapshot_state`\n(`src/rebar/_commands/compact.py:144`) splits tickets into \"lacking a `-SNAPSHOT.json`\" and\n\"already has one\", and only the former are compacted. A ticket that was folded once and has\nsince accumulated hundreds of live events counts as `already` and is never folded again — so\n`compact-all` is a one-time BACKFILL, not a recurring sweep.\n\nFix the selection, not the driver: count each ticket's FOLDABLE live events and select any\nticket whose foldable count exceeds `compact.threshold`\n(`src/rebar/_commands/compact.py:81`), whether or not a SNAPSHOT is present. Backfill becomes\nthe special case where the whole log is foldable. No new module, no second fold engine: the\nsnapshot semantics, horizon partitioning and authorship ledger in `compact_txn` are untouched.\n\nFOLDABLE, not merely live, is load-bearing. The fold only squashes events older than the\ncompaction horizon (`_compact_locked` partitions on `is_foldable`,\n`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:365`; horizon defaults to 1_800_000_000_000 ns =\n30 minutes, `src/rebar/_config_schema.py:332`). Selecting on the RAW live count would pick a\nticket whose excess events are all inside the horizon, the fold would return 0 having written\nnothing (\"all events within the compaction horizon — nothing to fold\"), the driver would count\nit as compacted, and the next sweep would select it again — non-converging churn plus a lying\ncount. So selection reuses the SAME predicate the fold uses, `is_foldable`\n(`src/rebar/_commands/_compact_policy.py`), reading the same configured horizon: the two agree\nby construction and cannot drift, the pattern this codebase already uses for shared decisions.\nAs a second guard the driver counts a ticket as compacted only when the fold actually wrote a\nSNAPSHOT, so a nothing-to-fold pass is reported honestly rather than as work done.\n\n**2. Trigger it out of band every 6 hours** (`cron: '0 */6 * * *'`), reusing the reconciler's\nproven recipe rather\nthan inventing a clone concept. `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` already runs a\nscheduled job that WRITES ticket events and pushes them to the `tickets` branch, from an\nephemeral runner that shares nothing with any interactive checkout. The new workflow copies\nits store-mount and identity steps verbatim in shape.\n\n*Clone lifecycle* — there is no long-lived clone to manage, which is the point:\n- **Create:** `actions/checkout` gives a fresh clone per run; the store is mounted with the\n  reconciler's exact steps (`reconcile-bridge.yml:126-130`) — full (non-shallow)\n  `git fetch origin '+tickets:refs/remotes/origin/tickets'`, `rm -rf .tickets-tracker`,\n  `git worktree add -B tickets .tickets-tracker origin/tickets`.\n- **Refresh:** each run re-derives the store from `origin/tickets`, so there is no stale state\n  to reconcile between runs. The tickets merge driver is configured\n  (`reconcile-bridge.yml:132-134`) so the push-retry loop can merge `origin/tickets` when the\n  branch moved mid-run.\n- **Retire:** the runner is disposable. A failed push leaves only local commits on a workspace\n  that is discarded; the next run starts from `origin/tickets` again and re-folds whatever is\n  still over threshold. Nothing accumulates, so there is no stale-clone cleanup class.\n\n*Signing and identity* — both resolve without bootstrapping anything new:\n- The bot git identity is configured as the reconciler does (`reconcile-bridge.yml:215-222`).\n- `secrets.REBAR_BOT_SIGNING_KEY` is materialized to a 0600 file and exported as\n  `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` (`reconcile-bridge.yml:233-248`); the inline signing seam signs\n  when that key resolves, and writes unsigned (advisory) when it does not — same posture as\n  reconciler writes today.\n- The environment identity needs NO bootstrap: `_seam.env_id`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:155`) reads `<tracker>/.env-id`, which is CONTENT of the\n  tickets branch, so a worktree of `origin/tickets` carries the store's own env id\n  automatically. This is why the sweep signs like any other writer of that store.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact.py` — threshold-based selection so `compact-all` recurs.\n- `.github/workflows/compact-sweep.yml` — new scheduled workflow (store mount + identity +\n  key materialization modeled on `reconcile-bridge.yml`), with `workflow_dispatch`.\n- `docs/concurrency.md` — record the 6-hourly trigger under the I9b section barbet added.\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_all_selection.py` — new selection tests.\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_sweep_races.py` — new convergence tests.\n\n## Testing\n- Selection: a ticket WITH a SNAPSHOT plus FOLDABLE events over threshold is selected; one\n  whose excess events are all inside the horizon is NOT (the churn case); one under threshold\n  is not; one with no SNAPSHOT (the backfill case) still is.\n- Double-snapshot race: two sweeps fold the same ticket from separate clones and both push;\n  the merged tracker reduces to the same state with no duplicate or lost events.\n- Mixed-version window: a sweep and a direct `rebar compact` fold the same ticket\n  concurrently; the SNAPSHOT-present short-circuit and `_sync_before_compact`\n  (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:52`) defer-to-remote converge them.\n- Concurrent tail: events appended while a fold runs replay on top of the SNAPSHOT.\n- Clone signing: a fold run from a fresh worktree of the tickets branch produces the same\n  authorship ledger and event signatures as an in-place fold.\n- Failure path: a rejected push leaves the local commits intact and reports the failure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `compact-all` selects an already-snapshotted ticket whose FOLDABLE event count exceeds\n      the threshold — a test seeds one, runs the sweep, and asserts it was folded.\n- [ ] The sweep converges: a ticket over threshold whose excess events are all inside the\n      compaction horizon is not selected, and if selected is not counted as compacted — a test\n      runs two consecutive sweeps and asserts the second reports zero compacted.\n- [ ] It still skips under-threshold tickets and still backfills snapshot-less ones — the same\n      test asserts both, so the change is a widening and not a replacement.\n- [ ] Two concurrent sweeps folding one ticket from separate clones converge — a test merges\n      both results and asserts identical reduced state with no duplicate or lost events.\n- [ ] Events appended during a fold survive it — a test asserts the tail replays on top of the\n      SNAPSHOT and appears in reduced state.\n- [ ] A fold run from a fresh tickets worktree signs identically to an in-place fold — a test\n      compares authorship ledger entries and event signatures.\n- [ ] The scheduled workflow exists with `cron: '0 */6 * * *'`, runs the sweep against a\n      mounted tickets worktree, and is `workflow_dispatch`-able; `docs/concurrency.md` records\n      that cadence, and the full local gate set plus CI's pytest tiers pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786604776646010001,"uuid":"49851304-ed99-4cde-be35-436dde376d41"}